{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443666-vtm-set-in-4th-century","id":1443666,"title":"VtM set in 4th Century","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-12T15:38:27-07:00","id":1443666,"title":"VtM set in 4th Century","content":"Hello-<br /> I am considering running a VtM game set in the 4th century, in the Roman empire. I will probably use Vampire Twentieth Anniversary Edition: The Dark Ages for the sake of simplicity and omit the Tremere for the Salubri. <br /> What other changes would you suggest? <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T16:21:32-07:00","id":1443669,"title":"","content":"Some of it might depend on where you are planning to set it. <br /> <br /> Two things though are that the Ravnos are likely seen as a predominantly Egyptian clan (via the Alexandrian Jati), with less noticeable Phaedymites primarily in Italy and Gaul. Then there's the extreme minority outliers of the Bashirites as a gnostic-Christian cult in Judea and the Sybarites as a small group of hedonists within Rome itself. <br /> The other is that the Assamites will have no association whatsoever whatever Islamic/Arabic stuff V20 material insists on focusing on (including &quot;othering&quot; them with a totally different name). They're going to be Christians, Jews, and followers of the Cult of Mithras, among other things, and in places like Greece and Alexandria, the scholar branch is likely to be the most common.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T16:40:25-07:00","id":1443671,"title":"","content":"Are you asking for mechanics changes only, or setting lore or intersection with real world history?<br /> <br /> Will this take place after the ascension of Constantine, but before the Battle of Adrianople?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T23:18:07-07:00","id":1443708,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturgy is going to be more common as an out-of-clan discipline, since the Tremere haven't monopolized it yet. There are going to be far fewer paths; Assamite sorcerers are talented but they're small in number and their organization leaves a bit to be desired. The Followers of Set are big on out-of-clan magic, but their religious way of doing things mean they're usually learning the same ceremonies rather than learning new spells, and they'd never learn, say, the Lure of Flames because the gods tied with that are firmly in the pocket of Ra (and also because they're weak to lights and flames make light). Paths are going to be rarer and a lot of the more independent magic styles not affiliated with a clan are going to be even more limited. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> makes a good argument for the Assamites, but i'd also go further to suggest that, as nasty vampires, many still follow older religions and encourage their neonates to do the same. The magic a few of them practice, Dur-An-Ki , has a somewhat antagonistic approach to the mainstream religions of this period (and will continue to do so). Ur Shulgi as a sorcerer isn't just being cartoonishly evil for wanting to purge foreign faiths from his clan, it's a practical move. (encouraging the Path of blood on the otherhand...) Dur-An-Ki itself is quite a divisive practice because it contains elements of both low magic (cooperating with spirits) and high magic (taking power from the stars) , and sorcerers may lean heavily one way or the other. The latter is more amicable to other faiths, while the former is seen as witchcraft. <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd leave necromancy as it is though. I'm not entirely familiar with this, but I recall something like the capadocians supposedly focusing on physical necromancy and only the giovanni came in and bothered with ghosts; That's pants. and hardly indicative of real world studies into death. Perhaps there would be less rituals and a few foreign paths would be harder to access; The capadocians are far, far less organized than the Giovanni after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-12T23:21:51-07:00","id":1443709,"title":"","content":"The few mechanical suggestions I have are simple things.<br /> <br /> 1. The farther back in time you go, the lower the default generations will be.<br /> 2. While Romans had excellent roads, travel at night is difficult in the ancient world, so you will be pretty much restricted to the cities, with a few exceptions.<br /> 3. Lupines and other shifters will be much more prevalent.<br /> 4. Mages will be stronger<br /> <br /> Beyond those adjustments, it really comes down to where the game is set and what sort of genre/theme you are running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T02:47:07-07:00","id":1443719,"title":"","content":"I'll throw out <i>Requiem for Rome</i> and<i> Fall of the Camarilla</i> as fantastic sources of inspiration. They're not only set during the Roman Empire, but the 4th century. Most of the material is translatable to Masquerade with a little tweaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T11:46:31-07:00","id":1443769,"title":"","content":"Isn't there a Storytellers Vault book called something like Vampires of antiquity or similar? Might be worth looking into that.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/336923/Vampire-Twentieth-Anniversary-Edition-The-Classical-Age?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/336923.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/336923/Vampire-Twentieth-Anniversary-Edition-The-Classical-Age?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire, Twentieth Anniversary Edition: The Classical Age - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/336923/Vampire-Twentieth-Anniversary-Edition-The-Classical-Age?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/336923/Vampire-Twentieth-Anniversary-Edition-The-Classical-Age?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Vampire, Twentieth Anniversary Edition: The Classical Age - &nbsp; The world of AD 62 is completely new for vampires. There has never been so much organization, but there has never bee </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T20:01:41-07:00","id":1443823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443666-vtm-set-in-4th-century?p=1443769#post1443769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't there a Storytellers Vault book called something like Vampires of antiquity or similar? Might be worth looking into that.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/336923/Vampire-Twentieth-Anniversary-Edition-The-Classical-Age?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr..._45624_0_0_0_0</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome book. Best VtM book I've read since Vampire: The Wild West.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T13:18:24-07:00","id":1444058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443666-vtm-set-in-4th-century?p=1443823#post1443823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Awesome book. Best VtM book I've read since Vampire: The Wild West.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The translation's a bit dodgy but the underlying game material is superb","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T13:41:38-07:00","id":1444064,"title":"","content":"I'd sit down with some other mythologies and make up alternative origins to the Abrahamic Caine mythos. I think that only got popular with the rise of the Abrahamic religons. The Setites have their own origin story, I'd stick with the ones that involve a kinslaying, like the Caine story and the Set/Osiris one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T23:58:36-07:00","id":1444309,"title":"","content":"As mentioned there's material to borrow/steal/mine in Requiem for Rome and Fall of the Camarilla. And I would also think that the Classical Age can give some stuff for you to use in some modified version due to the RfR's reliance on the Necropolis for Kindred society in Rome which I figure you may or may not be personally interested in including.<br /> <br /> Also you may not to decide what kind of game you want to run as different parts of the 4th century will offer very different frameworks in the case of the mortal world for your game to take place.<br /> <br /> EDITED<br /> <br /> And I should mention that if you want to make the Germanic tribes menacing the Romans a bit more nuanced to deal with you could take a passage from Requiem and move the Ventrue away from the Romans and into those Germanic tribes. Thus populating these northern tribes with both Ventrue and Gangrel in a tug-of-war for influence and perhaps allowing for more plots and interactions with these tribes, like for example the Goths. Of course this changes much but its an alternative if you want to shake things up and perhaps involved the &quot;barbarians&quot; more in the story.<br /> <br /> And I'll add a link to a resource that might be of use for you.<br /> <br /> The earliest take on Cainites in ancient Rome that I know about.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://vampiraroma.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://s0.wp.com/i/blank.jpg?m=1383295312i\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://vampiraroma.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampira Roma </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://vampiraroma.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://vampiraroma.wordpress.com/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Vampire: The Masquerade in Ancient Rome </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":". 04-17-2021, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T02:07:13-07:00","id":1444463,"title":"","content":"Change the weapons and armor list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-16T04:39:03-07:00","id":1448673,"title":"","content":"i would suggest to read V20: Vampire Classical Age from storytellersvault. Great work imho, It Is totally worth the Money. You can also find another Source Book written by italian people wich fouses on Rome. It Is called... Rome: Damnatio Memorie if I Remember correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26189-wuzaolover","name":"WuZaolover","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26189_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-17T01:55:57-07:00","id":1448761,"title":"","content":"Those are interesting times.<br /> <br /> In Roman Britain, Julius Cerialis decapitates his 4th generation Ventrue sire (I'd say Mithras didn't want competition); Montano used a Ravnos to appear the chi rho in the sky for Constantine to see; the Triumvirate is formed, Michael's famous speech to the Eternal Senate and Julia Antasia leaving the Eternal City; the embrace of Siegfried and then diablerie of Regulus; and, at last, Cretheus meets Saulot and become his student.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}